OL,6, The Home Secretary has agreed to
OL,7, another ban on marches - this time in
OL,8, South Yorkshire.
OL,10,FMr William Whitelaw backed a request
OL,11,Fby police for a one-week ban after
OL,12,Fa warning by the National Front that
OL,13,Fit intended to march tomorrow
OL,14,F"somewhere in Yorkshire".
OL,15,F
OL,16,FThe Assistant Chief Constable of the
OL,17,Farea, Mr Bob Goslin, said the Front
OL,18,Forganisers had deliberately not given
OL,19,Fdetails of their plans, and so it was
OL,20,Fimpossible for police to ensure the
OL,21,Fmaintenance of public order.
OL,23,T]CFromG21-03-80C/ teletextarchive.com
