OL,5, M  CSCOTLANDG 10-9CIRELAND
OL,8,FTorrents of rain made conditions
OL,9,Fsteadily worse - but both sides
OL,10,Fproduced a magnificent match.
OL,12,FDave Irwin put the visitors within one
OL,13,Fpoint after 53 minutes, after Scotland
OL,14,Fhad been 10-0 up at half time.
OL,16,FOllie Campbell started the fight back
OL,17,Fwith a penalty early in the second half
OL,19,FScotland's points came from a try by
OL,20,FHay and goals by Irvine and Rutherford,
OL,21,Fall scored within the first 22 minutes.
OL,23,T]CFromG21-03-80C/ teletextarchive.com
